---
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/breadcrumbs.astro'
import Link from '@/components/link.astro'
import PageHead from '@/components/page-head.astro'
import Layout from '@/layouts/layout.astro'
import { formatDate } from '@/lib/utils'

const lastUpdated = new Date('2026-04-01')
---

<Layout class="max-w-3xl">
  <PageHead slot="head" title="About" />

  <div class="flex flex-col gap-10">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'About', icon: 'lucide:info' }]} />

      <header class="flex flex-col gap-3 border-b border-border pb-8">
        <h1
          class="text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-4xl"
        >
          The man behind the screen
        </h1>

        <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">
          Last updated: {formatDate(lastUpdated)}
        </p>
      </header>
    </div>

    <article class="prose max-w-none">
      <p class="mt-0">
      I have always had a strong drive to understand complex ideas, optimize, and automate repetitive work. When I discovered programming, 
      I immediately felt at home. It is fractal by nature: each abstraction reveals new patterns, new problems, and new areas of expertise to master.

      I feel fortunate to be building in the current AI era, where new models and ideas emerge constantly. That pace keeps me learning and 
      pushes me to understand real-world limits so I can design systems that are both capable and reliable.
      </p>
      <p> 
I began my career in infrastructure project management, coordinating teams across infrastructure, security, telecom, and planning. 
While I enjoyed driving cross-functional execution, I wanted deeper technical ownership, which led me to transition into backend cybersecurity engineering. 
There, I designed and built systems and integrations that improved analyst productivity. 
In the same spirit of secure, trustworthy systems, I joined CoSAI, an open ecosystem focused on secure-by-design AI through shared standards, research, and guidance.
      </p>
      <p>
Today, I invest much of my time in SplitSound, a project I am building in public to make audio separation more reliable and simple for video creators. 
Outside of work, I love documenting nature trips with my DJI Neo 2 and 3D-printing accessories that improve my camping setup.     
</p>
     
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
